# Angular Modern Best Practices (Angular v20+)

This project adheres to modern Angular idioms, emphasizing maintainability, reactive signals, OnPush performance, accessibility, and modular design.

## TypeScript Best Practices

* **Strict Type Checking:** Always adhere to strict type checking. Catch errors at compile time.
* **Prefer Type Inference:** Allow TypeScript to infer types when they are obvious from context.
    * **Bad:**
        ```typescript
        let name: string = 'Angular';
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```typescript
        let name = 'Angular';
        ```
* **Avoid `any`:** Do not use `any`. Use `unknown` when a type is uncertain and narrow it safely with type guards.

## Core Component Standards

* **Standalone Components:** All components, directives, and pipes are standalone.
* **Implicit Standalone:** Do NOT add `standalone: true` inside `@Component`, `@Directive`, or `@Pipe` decorators. It is implicit and default in Angular v20+.
* **OnPush Change Detection:** Always set `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component decorator.
* **Host Object over Decorators:** Do NOT use `@HostBinding` or `@HostListener`. Define host bindings and event handlers inside the `host` property of the `@Component` or `@Directive` decorator:
    * **Bad:**
        ```typescript
        @HostBinding('class.active') isActive = true;
        @HostListener('click') onClick() { ... }
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```typescript
        @Component({
          // ...
          host: {
            '[class.active]': 'isActive()',
            '(click)': 'handleClick()',
          },
        })
        ```
* **Single Responsibility & Size:** Keep components small, focused, and single-purpose. Prefer inline templates (`template: ...`) for small components (< 30 lines) and external files for larger templates.

## Signals & Reactivity

* **Signal Inputs & Outputs:** Prefer `input()` and `output()` over `@Input()` and `@Output()`.
    * **Bad:**
        ```typescript
        @Input() userId!: string;
        @Output() userSelected = new EventEmitter<string>();
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```typescript
        import { input, output } from '@angular/core';

        userId = input.required<string>();
        userSelected = output<string>();
        ```
* **Two-Way Binding with `model()`:** Use `model()` instead of paired `@Input()` and `@Output()`.
    * **Bad:**
        ```typescript
        @Input() value = '';
        @Output() valueChange = new EventEmitter<string>();
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```typescript
        import { model } from '@angular/core';

        value = model<string>('');
        ```
* **Signal Queries:** Use `viewChild()` and `viewChildren()` instead of `@ViewChild` / `@ViewChildren`.
    * **Bad:**
        ```typescript
        @ViewChild('scrollContainer') container!: ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>;
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```typescript
        import { viewChild, ElementRef } from '@angular/core';

        container = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>>('scrollContainer');
        ```
* **Derived State with `computed()`:** Use `computed()` for any state derived from other signals. Keep computations pure, synchronous, and free of side effects.
* **Resettable / Linked State with `linkedSignal()`:** Use `linkedSignal()` when local writable state must recompute or reset whenever a source signal or input changes:
    * **Good:**
        ```typescript
        import { input, linkedSignal } from '@angular/core';

        options = input<string[]>([]);
        // Resets selectedOption to the first option whenever options() changes, but allows user selection
        selectedOption = linkedSignal(() => this.options()[0] ?? null);
        ```
* **Signal Mutations:** Always use `set(...)` or `update(...)`. Never mutate objects in place.
* **Side Effects:** Avoid `effect()` for state management or chaining state. Reserve `effect()` strictly for logging, analytics, or external imperative APIs (like Canvas or Audio).

## Templates & Control Flow

* **Native Block Control Flow:** Use `@if`, `@else if`, `@else`, `@switch`, `@case`, and `@for (...; track ...)`. Never use `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, or `*ngSwitch`.
    * **Bad:**
        ```html
        <div *ngIf="isVisible">Content</div>
        <div *ngFor="let item of items">{{ item.name }}</div>
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```html
        @if (isVisible()) {
          <div>Content</div>
        }
        @for (item of items(); track item.id) {
          <div>{{ item.name }}</div>
        }
        ```
* **Template Local Variables (`@let`):** Use `@let` to declare scoped template variables to avoid re-evaluating signals or complex expressions:
    * **Good:**
        ```html
        @let user = currentUser();
        @if (user) {
          <p>Welcome, {{ user.name }} ({{ user.role }})</p>
        }
        ```
* **Native Class and Style Bindings:** Do NOT use `ngClass` or `ngStyle`. Use native bindings:
    * **Bad:**
        ```html
        <div [ngClass]="{'active': isActive(), 'disabled': isDisabled()}"></div>
        <div [ngStyle]="{'width': width() + 'px'}"></div>
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```html
        <div [class.active]="isActive()" [class.disabled]="isDisabled()"></div>
        <div [style.width.px]="width()"></div>
        ```

## Services & Dependency Injection

* **`inject()` Function:** Prefer `inject()` over constructor injection for all dependencies:
    * **Bad:**
        ```typescript
        constructor(private rpcService: RpcService) {}
        ```
    * **Good:**
        ```typescript
        import { inject } from '@angular/core';

        private rpcService = inject(RpcService);
        ```
* **Single Responsibility & Scope:** Provide application singletons in root (`providedIn: 'root'`). Provide feature-scoped stores or view models at the feature component level.

## Unit Testing Signal Components

LPA policy: keep the UI suite **lean**—test regressions that can hurt users or data, not every widget. Scrutinize existing specs during review; remove or merge low-value tests. Details: `.cursor/rules/lpa-web-ui-tests.mdc` and Studio [lpa-web-ui-code-review.md](../../lpa-web-ui-code-review.md).

* **Setting Signal Inputs:** In tests, set signal inputs using `fixture.componentRef.setInput`:
    ```typescript
    fixture = TestBed.createComponent(MyComponent);
    fixture.componentRef.setInput('userId', 'user-123');
    fixture.detectChanges();
    ```
* **Mock Backend Services:** Always mock `ProjectInfoService`, `RpcService`, and `SessionService` in unit tests. Never allow specs to trigger actual HTTP or backend RPC calls.
